COT Flow falls in the medium-low range. It shares the same topical space as IBCD (5.33, Reject) and Consistency-FM (5.67, Reject) but has arguably more significant theoretical gaps (no collapse prevention mechanism, no output distribution constraint) and weaker baselines. However, it does have a genuine and interesting idea (OT-constructed COT pairs are novel and well-motivated) that produces empirical results. The two Major weaknesses (collapse/output distribution, outdated baselines) weigh heavily against acceptance but do not render the paper's contribution void. The paper is comparable to the medium-scoring rejected papers but somewhat weaker due to the theoretical gaps.

